{
  "format": 1,
  "about": "Account API behaviour, driven through each SDK's transport seam with canned responses. No case touches a network. Bodies are synthetic and shaped after measured responses - never recorded ones, because users/me and sub-users/ return live proxy passwords.",
  "html_page": "<!doctype html><html><head><title>NodeMaven</title></head><body><div id=\"root\"></div></body></html>",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "html-200-is-not-a-successful-delete",
      "origin": {
        "found": "2026-09-29",
        "by": "spec drafting",
        "published_unfixed": [
          "pypi nodemaven 0.1.4"
        ],
        "fixed": {
          "python": "2026-09-29, unreleased"
        }
      },
      "call": {
        "op": "delete_sub_user",
        "args": {
          "id": 1
        }
      },
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "body": "$html_page"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "error": "api"
      },
      "note": "dashboard.nodemaven.com answers an unregistered path 200 with its front end (measured 2026-09-09, 6415 bytes, byte-identical to a nonexistent path). A write that returns that page as its result reports a delete that did not happen."
    },
